= Electric Vehicle Cybersecurity
#link("https://me.utdallas.edu/faculty/jie-zhang/", ["Dr. Jie Zhang"])
Office: ECSW 3.150F
This project investigates the application of generative AI to enhance cybersecurity in electric vehicle (EV) charging and discharging systems. As EVs become increasingly integrated into smart grids and vehicle-to-grid (V2G) networks, they face growing risks from cyber threats targeting communication protocols, energy transactions and control systems. Students will explore how generative AI models can detect anomalies, simulate attack scenarios and develop adaptive defense mechanisms. The project will involve designing AI-driven monitoring tools, training models on synthetic and real-world data and evaluating their effectiveness in securing EV infrastructure. This research bridges AI, cybersecurity and sustainable transportation technologies.

= Custom build a 3D Bioprinter
#link("https://me.utdallas.edu/faculty/jiannan-li/", ["Dr. Jiannan Li"])
Office: ECSW 3.355A
Design and build a 3D bioprinter from scratch, with advanced features such as melt electrowriting or multi-material printing to be added.

= Self-Driving Lab
#link("https://me.utdallas.edu/faculty/connor-armstrong/", ["Connor Armstrong"])
Office: ECSW 4.355F
This project will develop a new approach to material development through the interplay of high-throughput, “self-driven” experimental characterization instruments and data-driven machine learning.
